# Default Components Only

Always use stock Nuxt UI (`U*`) and Vue/Nuxt built-ins as they ship. Never customize components. Layout and spacing must use inline Tailwind classes on `class`.

## Do

- Use default components: `UButton`, `UInput`, `UCard`, `UModal`, `UForm`, `UTable`, `UApp`, etc.
- Pass only documented props (`color`, `variant`, `size`, `label`, …).
- Put layout/spacing on the `class` attribute (Tailwind utilities).

```vue
<UButton color="primary" size="md" class="mt-4 w-full">ذخیره</UButton>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-4 p-6">
  <UCard class="w-full">
    <UInput v-model="name" class="w-full" />
  </UCard>
</div>
```

## Do not

- Do not wrap a default component just to restyle it.
- Do not use the `ui` / `:ui` prop, `class` slot overrides, or theme slot maps to restyle internals.
- Do not add `<style>` / `<style scoped>` for component look.
- Do not write custom CSS classes, `@apply`, or extra CSS files for UI.
- Do not fork or copy a `U*` component into `app/components` to change its markup or styles.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<UButton :ui="{ base: 'rounded-none bg-[#123]' }" />
<UButton class="my-special-btn" />
<style scoped>
.my-special-btn { background: #123; }
</style>
```
